Agent.text:
The app now has your OmniFind look, rebuilt from the OmniFind folder in the same layout, colours and fonts, and it picked up its main functions. It builds, and the screenshot check passes at 1280×820. The light and dark screenshots, the empty-results message and the drive filter look right. The tray icon, hotkey, single-instance behaviour, start-with-Windows and run-as-administrator were built but never run.

**Look:** I copied the custom title bar, the left sidebar and the search tabs from OmniFind, plus the large search card and the "Locations" and "Saved searches" panels. The results list, the inspector card and the five accent colours come from the same folder.

**Functions added:** these come from your OmniFind folder:
- clicking a drive filters results to it;
- a Ctrl+K command palette;
- a junk-folder filter;
- start with Windows;
- run as administrator;
- a single running copy;
- a global hotkey and close-to-tray;
- content search as a toggle.

**Not ported:** OmniFind's fast NTFS file-table indexing and its 2,500-row display cap. The app still does a normal folder scan and shows all results.
